course: dictionary
lesson: 7227
title: How plants make their own food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plants do not eat like we do. They make their own food, and the name for this process is photosynthesis. «Photosynthesis is how green plants make their own food.» Think of it as a recipe: the plant gathers ingredients and uses sunlight to cook them into sugar.
explain: The ingredients are water, carbon dioxide from the air, and sunlight. «Leaves use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide from the air into sugar for food; this is called photosynthesis.» The sugar is food for the plant, and most of the work happens in the leaves, in their green chlorophyll.
explain: Photosynthesis also gives us something we need. «Photosynthesis gives out oxygen into the air.» When you meet a new science word, read the words around it. The sentence tells you what the process does, so the clues help you understand the word.
fact: Photosynthesis is the way green plants make their own food using sunlight, water and carbon dioxide.
fact: Photosynthesis happens mainly in the leaves, in the green chlorophyll.
fact: Photosynthesis gives out oxygen, and that is the oxygen we breathe.
fact: In a simple word equation: carbon dioxide + water, with light and chlorophyll, makes glucose (sugar) + oxygen.
fact: A plant kept in the dark cannot photosynthesise, so it grows pale and weak.
exercise: «Photosynthesis is how green plants make their own food.» What is photosynthesis? | The way animals hunt for their food | The way leaves fall off trees in autumn | *The way green plants make their own food | A kind of green soil
exercise: Which ingredients does a plant need for photosynthesis? | Milk, meat and bread | Sugar, salt and oil | Soil, stones and sand | *Sunlight, water and carbon dioxide
exercise: «Photosynthesis gives out oxygen into the air.» What does photosynthesis give out? | Stones | *Oxygen | Sugar | Carbon dioxide
test: Where does photosynthesis mainly happen in a plant? | In the seeds | In the flowers | In the roots | *In the leaves, in the green chlorophyll
test: A plant is kept in a dark cupboard for weeks. What will happen to it? | It will make its own sunlight | *It will grow pale and weak, because it cannot photosynthesise | It will grow bigger and greener | It will grow flowers at once
exam: Read the words around «photosynthesis» in «Leaves use sunlight to turn water and carbon dioxide from the air into sugar for food; this is called photosynthesis.» What is the best meaning? | Animals breathing out gas at night | *Green plants using sunlight, water and air to make their own food | Plants being watered by people | Leaves changing colour in autumn
